Changes to the derived tests
T1 test_failures.py, test_health.py, test_policy_and_selection.py: aiohttp is not a zeocore dependency, so
   http_error() builds a stand-in exception with the same status, headers and text form instead of
   aiohttp.ClientResponseError. The classifier reads those attributes; the assertions are unchanged.
T2 the sys.path insertions are removed (the package is installed); the module names are rewritten.
T3 test_profile.py: an inline neutral profile replaces the tutorial JSON file that the upstream test read.
T4 test_engine_contract.py: contract.check takes an explicit source root; an empty root checks the lifecycle floor.
T5 test_failures.py: botocore is not a zeocore dependency; a stand-in ClientError carries the same response mapping.
T6 test_contract_scanner.py: the pure-scanner tests leave the installed-Rasa skip decorator.
Not copied (owned elsewhere): the tests for vendor sockets, the vendor catalogue, native NeuTTS, Rime, the Rasa
engine protocol and the installed-Rasa contract. See tests/test_voice/fixtures/audio/manifest.json for the fixtures.

Fixture provenance
The seven files under tests/test_voice/fixtures/audio/ are byte-identical to the upstream blobs listed below.
Upstream commit 739f447a (2026-09-02, "Regenerate fixture corpus with espeak-ng; correct the licence claims")
replaced them with speech synthesised by espeak-ng from the sentences in manifest.json, replacing an earlier
corpus made with macOS "say". The upstream generator, scripts/make_fixtures.py, is not carried into Core (its header explains the licence
reasoning). They are synthetic: no recorded human speech and no third-party speech corpus. Their licence is
Apache-2.0, as the rest of the derived files; this was checked in review.

